1
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:05,200
谁会后悔因为今天不帮我建鸭子村
Okay, who would hate to miss the chance of a lifetime

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,680
而错过这个千载难逢的机会呢
by not helping me build a duck village today?

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,040
这话好绕人啊
That was some tricky wording.

4
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,500
他想先绕晕我们再让我们帮忙
That's how he gets us.

5
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:13,560
我听懂了 我不会后悔因为不帮你
I got it -- I would not hate to miss

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:17,080
而错过这个千载难逢的机会
the chance of a lifetime by not helping you.

7
00:00:17,285 --> 00:00:18,720
但那只是因为我今天要工作
But only 'cause I have work.

8
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,000
我要上驾驶课
I've got a driving lesson.

9
00:00:20,211 --> 00:00:22,260
有事
Uh, something.

10
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:24,380
亲爱的 你好几周前就把这些蛋拿回来了
Honey, you found those eggs weeks ago,

11
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:26,120
到现在都还没孵化
and they still haven't hatched.

12
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,680
你难道不该做好心理准备接受
Should you prepare yourself for the possibility

13
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:30,700
这些蛋可能是...
that they might be...

14
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:31,320
鳄鱼蛋吗
Alligators?

15
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:32,600
-死了 -什么
- Dead. - What?!

16
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,400
你姐姐竟然说出这种话 你信吗
Can you believe your sister?

17
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:35,860
我信啊 已经死了
Yeah, I do. They're dead.

18
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:37,860
这件厨房里唯一已经死了的
The only thing that's dead in this kitchen

19
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:39,400
是你们孩童般的好奇心
is your childlike sense of wonder.

20
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,217
早上好 邓菲们
Morning, Dunphys.

21
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:42,720
鸭子还没出世哈
Oh, still no ducks, huh?

22
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,220
神奇的生物啊 我刚读了一本这方面的书
Fascinating creatures. I just read a book about them.

23
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:45,880
是吗
You did?

24
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:47,540
当然 老妈 迪兰看书的
Yes, mom. Dylan reads.

25
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:48,900
是我外甥的书
It was my nephew's book.

26
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,560
讲的是一只鸭子和一只企鹅
It was about a duck and a penguin

27
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:52,020
一起去度假
who go on vacation together.

28
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:53,940
你可以摸到鸭子的绒毛
You could touch the duck's fuzz.

29
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:54,580
哔哔[快进音效]
Bloop-bloop!

30
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:57,840
她想让我快进的时候就会发出这种声音
That's the sound she makes when she wants me to fast-forward.

31
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:58,820
我懂你
I feel you, money.

32
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:00,813
克莱尔也会这样对我
Claire does the same thing to me.

33
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:03,220
我觉得是从我发明那款新牙线开始的
I think it started when I was inventing that new dental floss.

34
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:04,060
哔哔
Bloop-bloop-bloop-bloop!

35
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,720
这本书上说鸭子从一出生开始
So, the book said ducklings imprint on their mom

36
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:07,740
就印刻它们的妈妈
as soon as they're born.

37
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:10,800
它们的脑子特别小 所以就依随着某样东西
Their brains are so small, they just latch on to something

38
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,880
然后牢牢跟着来获取食物
and follow it around as a way to find food.

39
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:14,060
好吃
Yum.

40
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:17,240
迪兰 我一会儿要建一个鸭子村
So, Dylan, I'm building a duck village later.

41
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:17,860
你想帮忙吗
You want to help?

42
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,660
这个问题好绕人
That's some tricky wording on that question.

43
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:22,840
他想帮忙 但是他还得...
He'd love to, but he's still --

44
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:25,380
时间到了 快煮毛巾
It's time! Boil some towels!

45
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:28,740
每次我吃鸡蛋你都要这样吗
Every time I have an egg? Really?

46
00:01:41,843 --> 00:01:43,160
塔克接住
Tucker goes deep!

47
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:43,280
小心
Watch it.

48
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:45,140
小卡
Cam!

49
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,219
慕奇有空位吗
Hut, hut, hut! Munch, you open?

50
00:01:47,219 --> 00:01:48,160
没人防他
Oh, he's open!

51
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:49,020
接球 接到了
Right there! There it is!

52
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:54,480
我们最近把楼上的房间租给了小卡原来大学里的
We have been renting the upstairs unit to some frat boys

53
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:55,680
脑残青年[兄弟会成员]
from Cam's old college.

54
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,260
他们来这里看比赛
They're here for some big game

55
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:59,840
顺便试试能不能上《购物街》节目
and to try and get on "The Price is Right."

56
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,980
但对我而言不幸的是
Unfortunately for me,

57
00:02:00,991 --> 00:02:04,260
这完全激发了小卡"梁山情义"的一面
it has brought out Cam's "Bromosexual" side.

58
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:05,760
-史诗级的传球啊 弟兄们 -赞
- Epic throw, bro. - Yeah!

59
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,700
其实这是羊绒上的传球
Actually, that is a cashmere throw,

60
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:09,140
现在上面有脚印了
which now has a footprint on it.

61
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:11,020
伙计们 来玩啤乓球吧
Dudes, beer pong!

62
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:12,120
乓 乓 乓
Pong, pong, pong!

63
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:13,340
啤酒在冰箱里 弟兄们
Beers are in the fridge, bros.

64
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,060
冰箱 冰箱 冰箱 冰箱
Fridge, fridge, fridge, fridge!

65
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:16,664
-不 等等 弟兄 -怎么了 亲爱的
- No, hang on, bro. - What's up, sweetie?

66
00:02:16,664 --> 00:02:17,640
你终于归位了
Oh, look who's back.

67
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:20,340
我发现你今天又请你朋友过来了呢
Um, so I see that you invited your friends again today.

68
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,820
是啊 他们是不是很好玩 你看杰斯多可爱
Yeah, aren't they fun? And how cute is Jace?

69
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:24,060
我们之前拉过手了
We held hands earlier.

70
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:25,600
其实是掰手腕 但还是算数啊
We were arm wrestling, but it still counts.

71
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:26,480
我们找到冰箱了
We found the fridge!

72
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,913
哟 你们做到了
Yo, you did!

73
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:30,880
那个就是杰斯
That's Jace.

74
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:32,520
到底有多少个杰斯
How many S's in 'Jace'? I heard 12.

75
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:34,880
我只是想让我们的客人开心些
I'm just trying to make our guests feel comfortable.

76
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,240
好了 来吧
All right, let's do this!

77
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:38,640
大爸为什么那样子说话
Why is Daddy talking like that?

78
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:39,400
婊疯矣[街头俚语]
She crazy.

79
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:49,340
好啦 怎么了啦
Ay, what is it?!

80
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,180
我不对劲的时候你总能看出来
You can always tell when something's wrong.

81
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,620
她叫什么
What is her name?

82
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:55,620
切尔西 是给我做过
Chelsea, the prettiest barista who's ever served me

83
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:57,440
双份半咖焦糖玛奇朵撒肉桂粉的
a double-shot half-caff caramel macchiato

84
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,460
最美的咖啡师
with a dusting of cinnamon.

85
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,180
我想搭讪她
I want to talk to her,

86
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:03,500
但我每次张口的时候 我就傻了
but whenever I do, all I can say is.

87
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:06,500
可能是因为你点咖啡时把词汇量都用完了
Maybe you used up all your words ordering that coffee.

88
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:08,140
你为什么这么害怕
Why are you so scared?

89
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:12,260
能看到你那双美丽的眼睛 听到你甜美声音的女人
Any woman would be so lucky to look into those beautiful eyes

90
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:14,480
是多么的幸运
and listen to that sweet voice.

91
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,300
-她是如此地... -我的节目开始了
- She's so -- - My show is on!

92
00:03:20,299 --> 00:03:22,042
真美啊
Ay, que linda...

93
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,040
玛瑞拉·莫纳拉斯是我最爱的女演员
Mariela Morales is my favorite actress,

94
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:26,020
她要用卡梅丽塔·孔特雷拉斯这个假名
and she's staying in a hotel in town

95
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:28,340
住在城里的一处酒店里
under the fake name Carmelita Contreras.

96
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,860
我要在大厅里等她
I am going to wait for her at the lobby,

97
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:32,840
我知道我听起来像个跟踪狂
and I know I sound like a stalker,

98
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,360
但是这不一样
but -- but this is very different,

99
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,740
因为我们一见面就会像闺蜜一样
because when we meet, we're going to be best friends.

100
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:39,160
我仿佛已经能闻到她的发香
I can already smell her hair.

101
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:40,680
好了 广告时间
Okay, commercials.

102
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,900
所以你应该这样
So, this is what you're going to do.

103
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:45,700
首先 你要带我去酒店见玛瑞拉
First you're gonna take me to the hotel to meet Mariela.

104
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:47,655
我要请她今晚来家里吃饭
I'm gonna invite her over for dinner tonight.

105
00:03:47,655 --> 00:03:49,020
她五点要参加一个慈善活动
She has a charity event at 5:00,

106
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,300
但他们不管饭
but they're not serving food.

107
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,300
-跟踪狂 -我跟玛瑞拉在一起的时候
- Stalker. - While I'm with mariela,

108
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:54,140
你就回去找你的咖啡女孩
you're gonna go back to your coffee girl

109
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:56,580
你要给她机会让她认识你
and you're gonna give her the chance to get to know you.

110
00:03:56,608 --> 00:03:58,139
你真的觉得我...
You really think I --

111
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:59,160
广告结束了
Commercial is over.

112
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,460
-又是这个剧吗 -是的
- This show again? - Yes.

113
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:04,440
我不知道这是什么剧 但我好爱这个角色
I don't know what it is. I love this character so much.

114
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:07,380
那个老家伙是谁
Who's the old crank?

115
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:08,980
当然是她老公了
Her husband, of course.

116
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:13,320
那个戴围巾的是个什么鬼
Who's the disaster with the scarf?

117
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,480
她儿子 佩皮托
Her son, Pepito.

118
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:17,420
你跟那个人至少还长得像
You at least look like your guy.

119
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:18,980
-我那个人... -是吗 佩皮托
- My guy -- - Can it, Pepito.

120
00:04:21,020 --> 00:04:21,700
亲爱的
Hey, honey.

121
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,000
你能看得清吗
Can you read that?

122
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:24,980
-嘎嘎尼科尔森 -太好了
- "Quack Nicholson". - Oh, good.

123
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:26,680
我花了一早上漆这个迷你鸭子信箱
If I spent the whole morning painting these

124
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,400
结果要是没人能看得清
tiny duck mailboxes and no one could read them,

125
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,660
那我岂不是傻了吗
I'd feel pretty ridiculous.

126
00:04:31,638 --> 00:04:33,000
菲尔 鸭食[邓菲]
Phil, duck feed!

127
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,500
听起来好像我的名字
Hey, that's almost my name.

128
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:35,820
你是不是该说对不起
Or "I'm sorry"?

129
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:37,540
你说的没错 对不起 我...
You're right. I'm sorry. I'll, uh --

130
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:38,760
我一会儿就把它扫干净
I'll sweep that up in a minute.

131
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,520
过来帮我把身上掸干净
Just come over here and help dust me off.

132
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:41,480
我有个重要会议
I've got an important meeting,

133
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:43,940
我不能带着满身亚麻籽去上班
And I can't go into the office covered in flaxseed.

134
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:45,820
这其实是燕麦 毛毛虫以及蟋蟀
It's actually a proprietary blend

135
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:47,500
按一定比例混合的独家配方
of oats, grub worms, and cricket parts.

136
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:49,380
-掸干净 -对不起
- And we're dusting. - Yeah, sorry.

137
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,600
你不是在为今天的会议感到紧张吧
Yeah. You're not nervous about the meeting today, are you?

138
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:52,380
我是很紧张
Yeah, I am.

139
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:54,720
这是我第一次在我爸和他那自大的设计团队面前
This is the first time I'm pitching closet-design ideas

140
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:57,200
做有关橱柜设计想法的演讲
to my dad and his pretentious creative team.

141
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,840
你说的是圣诞派对上拄着拐棍的
You mean the young guys with the walking sticks

142
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,220
-那些年轻人吗 -是啊
- at the Christmas party? - Yes.

143
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:03,280
他们觉得总部里的人比不上他们
They don't think anybody in corporate can do what they do,

144
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:04,720
可我的想法很好
but my ideas are good.

145
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:06,220
或者很烂
Or they suck.

146
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,620
我来开门
I've got it!

147
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:10,160
你的想法肯定很棒 别怀疑自己
I'm sure your ideas are great. Stop doubting.

148
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,720
你越相信自己 他们也会越相信你
The more you believe in yourself, the more they will.

149
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:14,500
谢谢
Thank you.

150
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:15,480
学霸好
Hey, nerds.

151
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,440
别介意
Ignore this.

152
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:19,920
你想让我帮你做的
So, what's this super-fun project

153
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:20,780
"超级有趣"的项目是什么
you want me to help you with?

154
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:22,560
我们要建一个鸭村
We are building a duck village.

155
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:24,700
妈
Um, hey, Mom,

156
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,840
我的驾校教练说今天不能上课了
My driving instructor just canceled on me.

157
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,860
真糟 好吧 我来做你的教练
Oh, shoot, fine. Fine, I'll take you.

158
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:30,920
真糟 好吧 我坐后座
Oh, shoot, fine. I'll sit in the back.

159
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:32,280
不 不 你留在这里帮菲尔
No, no, no. You're gonna stay here and help Phil.

160
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,740
我们去见你的表亲们
Let's go meet your cousins.

161
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:35,460
谢啦 米奇尔舅舅
Well, thanks, Uncle Mitch.

162
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:35,940
好
Yeah.

163
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,920
你知道卢克路考已经两次没过了吧
You know Luke has failed that driver's test twice now, right?

164
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:43,340
我今天能选的只有脑残屋 鸭村或者车祸
My options today are frat house, duck village, or car crash.

165
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:45,120
我觉得我的选择没问题
I'm feeling very comfortable with my decision.

166
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,620
这些灯是干什么的啊
What are you doing with those lights?

167
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:49,160
我想给这些蛋升温
I'm trying to get some heat on these eggs.

168
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,340
由于和普通商品弄混
Due to a grocery mishap,

169
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:51,960
它们不幸在冰箱里待了几个小时
they spent about seven minutes in the fridge.

170
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:54,160
他一个月前发现了这些蛋
So, uh, eggs he found a month ago,

171
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:56,080
又要给它们建一个鸭村...
building a whole village for them now...

172
00:05:56,786 --> 00:05:58,440
家里一切都还好吧
How's everything at home? Okay?

173
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:03,300
我们有一些关于这些鸭子是否存活的探讨
There is some debate as to the alive-ness of the ducklings.

174
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,420
但我得说
But I have to say,

175
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:08,000
与抱着那种信念和乐观的人一起生活
living with that kind of belief and optimism,

176
00:06:08,010 --> 00:06:09,003
真是没法不受影响啊
it just rubs off on you.

177
00:06:09,003 --> 00:06:10,543
我只想...
I am just gonna...

178
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:12,820
这应该能让我的这些蛋[蛋蛋]保持温暖
This should keep my eggs warm.

179
00:06:18,523 --> 00:06:21,540
你怎么这么安静 我做错什么了吗
You are just so quiet. What am I doing wrong?

180
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:21,760
没什么
Nothing.

181
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:23,820
安静会让我紧张
Silence makes me nervous.

182
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,340
说点什么吧
Talk about something.

183
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,480
聊聊你今天过得如何
Tell me about your day.

184
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:27,671
好吧
Uh, okay.

185
00:06:27,671 --> 00:06:29,720
今天早上 起床的时候
Well, this morning, uh, I woke up

186
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:31,400
差点被一个橄榄球打断鼻梁
and almost got my nose broken by a football.

187
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:33,640
我们楼上住了几个脑残青年
We have some frat guys staying upstairs,

188
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:35,720
小卡经常跟他们一起玩
and Cam hangs out with them a lot.

189
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:37,474
你不喜欢吗
And you're not okay with that?

190
00:06:37,474 --> 00:06:39,559
我不知道 也许吧
I don't know. I-I guess.

191
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:40,920
谁会在意
Who cares?

192
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:42,840
拜托 让我切进去[说给我听听]
Come on, let me in.

193
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:44,142
好吧 坦白讲
Okay, if I'm being honest,

194
00:06:44,142 --> 00:06:46,405
小卡的行为让我感觉很尴尬
I find Cam's behavior a little embarrassing,

195
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:48,540
主要是他说的那些"哟"啊"弟兄"啊
You know, with all of his "Yos" and "bros".

196
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:49,480
省省吧
I mean, calm down.

197
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:50,720
你一个中年基大叔
You're a middle-aged gay man

198
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:52,440
就不要边说话边扭屁股了
who punctuates sentences with your hip.

199
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:54,260
终于切进来[说出来]
Finally.

200
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:57,320
就是啊 承认这一点感觉真舒服
I know. It feels good to admit it, you know?

201
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:01,620
走吧[继续说]
Go on.

202
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:03,140
你知道还有什么很烦人吗
You know what else is really irritating?

203
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:05,440
他多渴望跟他们在一起
How needy he is with them.

204
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,300
让我进去
Let me in.

205
00:07:10,178 --> 00:07:11,120
怎么了 弟兄
What up, bro?

206
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:13,200
你们没意识到你们有多吵吗
Do you seriously not know how loud you're being?

207
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,513
邻居全都在抱怨
The neighbors are complaining.

208
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:19,280
我尊重你们 你们却完全不尊重我
I give you guys respect, and you give me nothing.

209
00:07:20,113 --> 00:07:21,940
我是说 我们...
I mean, we -- we --

210
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:22,820
骗到你们了
Got you!

211
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:24,180
什么
What?

212
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:26,340
你们真该看看你们那样子
You should have seen your faces.

213
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:27,071
你们一脸 "不是吧
You were like, "What?

214
00:07:27,071 --> 00:07:30,154
我 我们真的很对不起"的表情
W-we -- we really are j-just so sorry!"

215
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:31,743
-骗到我们了 -这一招不错吧 弟兄们
- You got us. - That was a good one, bro.

216
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:32,707
你真该跟我们来几杯
You got to do shots with us.

217
00:07:32,707 --> 00:07:33,840
-好吧 -慕奇 去拿野格酒
- Okay. - Munch, get the jaeger.

218
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:36,160
我们是不是应该拿小纸杯来喝
Yeah, should we serve the potion in cups of dixie?

219
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,740
-或者... -别废话 赶紧去拿吧
- Or the -- - Just get it, dude.

220
00:07:37,740 --> 00:07:38,640
好
Yeah.

221
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,220
我刚想到了一个超屌逼的主意
I just had the sickest idea.

222
00:07:40,907 --> 00:07:43,252
卡罪犯应该加入我们的任务
Caminal should join our mission.

223
00:07:43,284 --> 00:07:45,239
卡罪犯是谁 是我吗
Who's caminal? Am I -- am I caminal?

224
00:07:45,239 --> 00:07:46,919
你们想让我加入你们的任务吗
You want -- you want me to go on a mission?

225
00:07:46,919 --> 00:07:49,021
当然啦 你屌得飞起 老兄
Of course! You're auto-bid, dog.

226
00:07:49,021 --> 00:07:50,680
好吧 任务是什么
Okay, what is this mission?

227
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,340
先喝酒
This first.

228
00:07:51,350 --> 00:07:54,334
为您呈现的是 至高无上的野格酒
Presenting Lord and Lady Jaeger.

229
00:07:54,344 --> 00:07:55,720
闻起来应该是这个味儿吗
Does this smell the way it's supposed to smell, or...

230
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,260
酒不多了 所以我混了一下
We were low, and I had to mix.

231
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:59,814
为您呈现的是 至高无上的野格-奎沃-韦泽酒
Presenting Lord and Lady Jaeger-Cuervo-Weiser.

232
00:07:59,814 --> 00:08:01,412
小卡 小卡 小卡
Cam! Cam! Cam!

233
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:12,500
基本想法就是以上这些
So, that's just the rough idea.

234
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,060
如果想要看更多草图
If you want to see more sketches,

235
00:08:14,073 --> 00:08:17,060
可以去我的"橱柜云"账户
just check out my ClosetCloud account.

236
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:19,480
虽然我只是公司的一员
Um, look, I know I'm just a suit in this company,

237
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:21,780
但我还是要说 我感到有点失望
But I've got to say, I'm a little underwhelmed.

238
00:08:21,780 --> 00:08:24,100
-我喜欢这想法 -因各位的反应而失望
- I love it. - By the reaction from the rest of you suits.

239
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:25,640
拜托 我们是一家人
Come on, we're a family. Right?

240
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:28,840
亲爱的 我们可以去跟乔治·罗斯聊了吗
So, honey, are we all set for our pitch with George Ross

241
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,220
-就在今天下午 -好的 先生
- this afternoon? - Yes, sir.

242
00:08:30,231 --> 00:08:31,460
我之前不是让你别叫我"亲爱的"了吗
What did I tell you about "honey"

243
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:32,440
-抱歉 -不要在公司里叫
- Sorry. - At the office?

244
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,745
好吧 如果没有其它事情...
Okay, so, if there's nothing else --

245
00:08:33,756 --> 00:08:35,660
其实 如果你们不介意
Actually, um, if -- if you don't mind,

246
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:37,840
我想展示一下我自己的设计
I'd like to show you some designs of my own.

247
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:40,900
总部的人现在也会展示新设计了吗
So, corporate is pitching creative ideas now?

248
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,120
我知道我看起来不像那种
I know I don't look like

249
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:44,140
踩滑板上班的人
I just rode to work on my skateboard.

250
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:45,660
完了 说到你了
Snap. Look at you.

251
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:48,720
但对需要专门脱离盒外思考[创新思维]的人群来说
But for people who are paid to think outside the box,

252
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:52,040
你们却依旧束缚于盒子内部
you people are pretty inside the box

253
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:56,640
而这盒子正是我们所说的"伟大的衣柜"
when it comes to the box we call the mighty closet.

254
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:58,700
-关灯 -看来她是玩真的
- Lights. - So I guess we're doing this.

255
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,900
我想称这款衣橱为"大使先生"
I like to call this model the Ambassador.

256
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:04,689
在我们的皇室复兴系列大获成功之后
After the success of our royal renaissance series,

257
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:08,660
我在想 挂衣杆为什么不用黄铜杆呢
I thought, "Why not brushed brass for the valet rods?"

258
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:09,860
已经试过了 开灯
Been done. Lights.

259
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:11,470
什么 我没太明白
What? I'm, I'm sorry.

260
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,620
五年前就试过了 没什么用
We tried it five years ago. It didn't work.

261
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,440
这种杆子挂不住丝质衣物
Silk shirts slip off the brass.

262
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:19,160
我才刚开始呢
Okay. Well, I'm just getting started.

263
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:19,640
关灯
Lights.

264
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:23,920
这种样板有一个特殊的隐藏式收纳柜
This model features a hidden tilt-out hamper.

265
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:26,180
-这主意很棒 -谢谢您的赞同
- That's a terrific idea. - I'm glad you think so.

266
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:28,040
当肯·萨顿在1992年提出这个想法时
Is what Ken Sutton's boss told him

267
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,720
他的老板也是这么认为的
when he pitched it in 1992.

268
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:30,380
开灯
Lights.

269
00:09:31,058 --> 00:09:32,600
你得精通衣柜发展史啊
You've got to know your history.

270
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:33,340
真的
Honestly.

271
00:09:33,389 --> 00:09:34,260
我懂了
So, it's --

272
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:36,660
你想看的是原创衣柜
it's originality you're looking for.

273
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,700
你没搞错吧 花这么大功夫
You're not seriously coming in here,

274
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:40,840
就给我看田纳西推拉门
pitching me the Tennessee slider.

275
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:43,860
你就只有这些想法吗
Is that the best you've got?

276
00:09:46,009 --> 00:09:46,999
那就收工吧
Okay, I think we're done here.

277
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:52,200
老妈
Hey, Mom.

278
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:53,320
曼尼
Oh, hi, Manny.

279
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,760
你跟那个女孩怎么样了
How did it go with your coffee girl?

280
00:09:55,773 --> 00:09:57,360
我们相处得很棒 真的 我
Really great, actually. Yeah, I--

281
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,280
-你在骗我 -你怎么知道
- You're lying. - How could you tell?

282
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,680
我不知道 你刚刚承认的
I couldn't. You just confessed.

283
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:02,980
我走向柜台 然后就紧张了
I got up to the counter and panicked.

284
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:04,580
我买了两张圣诞专辑
I bought two Christmas CDs,

285
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:06,360
一个根本不吃的松饼 然后走了
a muffin I didn't need, then left.

286
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:08,600
曼尼 鼓起勇气跟她说话啊
Manny, please just talk to her.

287
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,720
她跟其他人一样啊 你是怎么了
She's like everybody else. What's wrong with you?

288
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:12,260
妈 我又不是你
Mom, I'm not you.

289
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:15,140
我走进房间时 周围的人不会转身看我
When I walk into a room, everyone's head doesn't turn.

290
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:17,520
我说笑话的时候他们也不会捧场笑得特别开心
People don't laugh extra hard at my jokes.

291
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:20,320
这个世界对你这样的美女总是格外善良
The world is different for people like you.

292
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,860
可是曼尼
Manny, but you --

293
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:23,800
别说了 我不想说这事
I don't, really don't want to talk about it anymore.

294
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:26,220
你还是快去吧 不然她就走了
You better hurry. You're gonna miss your chance.

295
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,880
别走开
Okay, stay right here.

296
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:28,740
我马上就回来
I'll be right back.

297
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:30,780
玛瑞拉 玛瑞拉·莫纳拉斯
Mariela! Mariela Morales!

298
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:31,620
什么事
Si?

299
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:32,100
你好
Hola!

300
00:10:34,855 --> 00:10:37,208
玛瑞拉
Ma-mariel--

301
00:10:38,003 --> 00:10:39,489
我是怎么了
Ay, what's wrong with me?

302
00:10:39,489 --> 00:10:40,830
玛瑞拉
M-mariel...

303
00:10:47,414 --> 00:10:48,962
有人点了六个大份披萨吗
Somebody order six large pizzas?

304
00:10:48,962 --> 00:10:51,170
谁来付一下钱
Hey, uh, somebody pay the pizza guy.

305
00:10:53,791 --> 00:10:54,462
你们有事吗
Can I help you?

306
00:10:54,462 --> 00:10:56,144
我们是来参加派对的
Uh, yeah. We're here for the party.

307
00:10:56,144 --> 00:10:57,857
我们应该在名单上
We should be on the list.

308
00:10:57,857 --> 00:10:58,724
不好意思
Aw, yeah, my bad.

309
00:10:58,724 --> 00:11:00,003
有那么一秒 我还以为你们是
Yeah, see, for a second, I thought you guys

310
00:11:00,003 --> 00:11:02,108
伊利诺伊来的混球
were just a couple Illinois douches

311
00:11:02,108 --> 00:11:03,161
你们以为我会那么蠢
who thought that I'd be dumb enough

312
00:11:03,161 --> 00:11:04,678
让你们若无其事地走进来
just to let you walk in --

313
00:11:05,514 --> 00:11:06,628
搞什么
What the hell?!

314
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:08,032
快走
Go!

315
00:11:08,032 --> 00:11:09,094
快走
Go, go!

316
00:11:10,746 --> 00:11:12,231
在约好的地方见
Meet at the rendezvous!

317
00:11:14,285 --> 00:11:16,287
这里是邮局
So, this is the post office,

318
00:11:16,287 --> 00:11:19,269
不然它们就收不到账单[喙]了
cause where else are they gonna get their "bills"?

319
00:11:19,785 --> 00:11:21,890
当然了 你得绕开这个人
Of course, you got to waddle past this guy

320
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:23,748
才能去做指甲
to get to the nail salon.

321
00:11:23,748 --> 00:11:28,722
街旁边要新开一家混合健身中心
And word on the street is they're putting in a CrossFit next door.

322
00:11:28,722 --> 00:11:30,889
这两个蛋怎么粘粘的
Why are these two eggs sticky?

323
00:11:30,889 --> 00:11:33,407
因为邻居家的狗很不老实
Because the neighbor's dog is a real slobberer,

324
00:11:33,407 --> 00:11:34,934
不过还好我动作快
but lucky, he's not very fast.

325
00:11:34,934 --> 00:11:37,782
我老师告诉我们 说一个人是怪胎是不对的
My teacher says that there's no such thing as weird,

326
00:11:37,782 --> 00:11:38,659
他们只是不一样而已
just different.

327
00:11:38,659 --> 00:11:41,187
你从哪冒出来这个想法的 不过说得很对
That's a lovely random thought.

328
00:11:41,187 --> 00:11:42,869
我画了好几种鸭金汉宫的修建草图
I drew up plans for a Duckingham Palace,

329
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:43,798
不过我找不到图纸了
but I can't find them,

330
00:11:43,808 --> 00:11:46,945
看来我们只能现场发挥[翅膀]了
so I guess we'll just have to "wing" it.

331
00:11:47,338 --> 00:11:48,411
那是什么东西
What the heck is that?

332
00:11:48,411 --> 00:11:51,620
是能让小鸭子觉得安全的鸭叫声
Oh, it's a duck call to make the ducklings feel safe.

333
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:53,820
我是不是该找个真正的大人过来
Should there be another adult present?

334
00:11:54,140 --> 00:11:54,580
不用
No.

335
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:56,040
不过这里应该有个小孩
But there should be a kid present.

336
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:56,920
你就是那个小孩
That kid is you.

337
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:59,460
你以后翻白眼的日子还多着呢
You've got your whole life to roll your eyes.

338
00:11:59,540 --> 00:12:01,280
今天我们不只是建造一个鸭子村而已
Today isn't just about building a duck village.

339
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:03,140
更是要让你学会微笑
It's about building your smile.

340
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:04,380
别抗拒
Don't fight it.

341
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:06,720
终于笑了
There it is.

342
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,680
正如你看到的
As you can see,

343
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:11,980
我们的鸭村港口有一座正在亮灯的灯塔
our little duck harbor has a working lighthouse.

344
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,720
等等 他刚才说了什么
Wait a second, what in the world did he just say?

345
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:15,580
一座亮灯的灯塔 没错 灯亮着呢
A working lighthouse? Yes, it is working.

346
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:17,940
很棒对吧
Pretty cool, huh?

347
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:19,480
别激动 莉莉
Easy, easy, Lily.

348
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:21,760
忘记掉你听过的一切关于蛋的传闻
Forget everything you've ever heard about eggs.

349
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,380
它们其实很易碎
They're actually quite delicate.

350
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,660
你得很小心 不好
You've got to be very care-- son of a -- aah!

351
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:26,440
完蛋了
Oh, no!

352
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:29,360
好烫
Hot!

353
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:33,400
看
Look.

354
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:34,700
有蛋叛逃了
We've got a runner!

355
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:36,880
不
No!

356
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:40,940
太好了 还跟新的一样
Hey, good as new.

357
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:43,740
婊疯矣
She crazy.

358
00:12:47,260 --> 00:12:50,620
他让我在自己家觉得像个外人...
He makes me feel like an outsider in my own home, and...

359
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:52,520
现在这么一说 我突然想起来
Now that I think about it,

360
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:54,820
自从我们把楼上的公寓租出去后...
ever since we started renting that upstairs apartment...

361
00:12:54,830 --> 00:12:56,000
我们真的要绕远路[扯太远]吗
Do we want to take this detour?

362
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,020
不 这跟我接下来要说的有关
No, it's relevant. Stay with me.

363
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:59,280
不仅仅是那些脑残青年的问题
It's not just the frat boys. No.

364
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:00,740
他对所有的租客都这样
He's this way with all of our guests.

365
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:02,380
小卡换床单
Cam doesn't change the sheets

366
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:04,060
都不如他换性格换得勤
as much as he changes his personality.

367
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:05,580
好了 女士们
All right, ladies.

368
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:07,540
我们已经准备好了热茶
We got some steaming-hot tea,

369
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:08,960
以及新鲜出炉的饼干
some popping-hot biscuits.

370
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,540
那么现在 让我们来好好唠一唠
Now, let's have a little sizzling-hot gossip.

371
00:13:13,339 --> 00:13:14,863
-别进去 -别啊
- Do not go in there! - Don't!

372
00:13:14,873 --> 00:13:17,083
不要开 我的天
Do not open -- oh, my god!

373
00:13:17,083 --> 00:13:19,595
不要 姑娘 不要再回去
No! Girl, do not go back in there!

374
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:23,320
我就是觉得小卡做得太过了
I just think Cam tries too hard.

375
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:25,000
就好像他在求着别人喜欢他一样
It's like he's begging to be liked.

376
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:27,480
等等 这是条单行道[光是一个人的错]吗
Wait, is this a one-way street?

377
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,860
这个问题问得好
Oh, that's a fair question.

378
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:32,780
我猜我还是应该试着努力跟人相处
I don't -- I guess I could make more of an effort with people.

379
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:33,720
我只是
I just --

380
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,720
根本就不擅长这些
It doesn't exactly come naturally to me.

381
00:13:43,022 --> 00:13:44,560
-小卡 -小卡
- Oh, Cam! - Cam!

382
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:46,980
就连对着两个红发律师我也没啥可说
I couldn't even find anything to say to two red-headed lawyers.

383
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:48,680
-我找不到路了[没听明白] -抱歉
- I'm lost. - I know.

384
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:49,580
我扯远了
I'm all over the place.

385
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:51,600
也许我只是在嫉妒
I think that I'm just maybe jealous

386
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:53,560
他能跟所有人打成一片
that he can hit it off with anybody.

387
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:55,960
但我不能因为他人见人爱就生他气
But I can't be mad at him for being likable.

388
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,000
毕竟这也是我爱上他的原因之一
I mean, that's one of the reasons I fell in love with him.

389
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:58,620
是小卡吗
Cam?

390
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:00,020
不然你以为我在说谁
Who else would I be talking about?

391
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,960
不是 那个牵着山羊的披萨外卖哥
No, the pizza guy with the goat

392
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:02,940
看着很像小卡叔叔
looks like Uncle Cam.

393
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:05,840
好吧 这肯定又是出了什么状况
Okay, I feel like there's a story here.

394
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:07,600
亲爱的
Hey, honey.

395
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,180
我不想说话
I don't want to talk about it.

396
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,440
好 看在我们"夫夫"一场的份上
Okay, for the sake of our marriage,

397
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,060
我猜这肯定跟那群脑残青年有关
I'm gonna assume that this is frat-related.

398
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,700
那不是我送你的皮带吗
Oh, look -- the belt I got you.

399
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:16,600
好了 靠边停一下
Okay, pull over.

400
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,240
小卡 你能不能先停一下
Cam, could you just stop for a second?

401
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:23,820
拜托 停一下嘛
Come on, stop.

402
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:25,240
我很抱歉
Look, I'm sorry.

403
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:28,560
抱歉在过去几周 我一直对你翻白眼
For the past few weeks, I've been rolling my eyes at you,

404
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:30,480
觉得你病态地
thinking that you had this pathological need

405
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,620
想要得到所有人的喜爱
to be liked by everyone,

406
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,840
但是我真是大错特错
but I couldn't have been more wrong.

407
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:35,140
你是天生招人喜欢
All right? People are just drawn to you.

408
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:36,960
不 我的确是病态地想要被喜欢
No, I do have a pathological need to be liked.

409
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:39,280
-我就知道 -这是个玩过火的白痴恶作剧
- I knew it. - This is a stupid prank gone wrong,

410
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,420
而我 我也和那群哥们儿走散了
and I've -- I'm separated from the guys.

411
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:44,140
为了让他们喜欢我 我甚至偷了一只山羊
I wanted them to like me so much I stole a goat.

412
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:47,440
我成了偷羊贼了 米奇尔
I'm a rustler, Mitchell.

413
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,420
一个十恶不赦的偷羊贼
I'm a filthy rustler.

414
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:51,400
在我看来并没有这么糟
Okay, well, that seems worse to you than it does to me.

415
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:52,280
对每一届房客我都是这德行
I do it with all of our guests.

416
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:53,360
我改变了自我
I change who I am

417
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,500
就为了让他们能更喜欢我
so they'll like me more.

418
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,400
-这样好累 -那就别再继续了
- It's exhausting. - Well, then, stop.

419
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:59,060
因为你本来的样子已经足够招人喜欢
Because you're likable enough just being you.

420
00:14:59,060 --> 00:14:59,800
我知道
I know.

421
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:02,720
我讨厌自己有这种不安全的感觉
And this insecurity is a part of me that I do not love.

422
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:05,224
-卡罪犯 -弟兄们好啊
- Caminal! - What's up, my brothers?!

423
00:15:05,224 --> 00:15:06,909
-小卡 -我到底是怎么了
- Cam. - What is wrong with me?

424
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:08,660
快上车 我们还要涂山羊呢
Get in -- we got a goat to paint!

425
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:10,272
不 听着 各位
No, you know what, guys?

426
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:11,680
这样不对
This isn't right.

427
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:12,980
我不是这样的人
This is not who I am.

428
00:15:13,180 --> 00:15:14,640
所以我要把山羊还回去
So I'm gonna take the goat back,

429
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:16,920
如果你们是真朋友 你们会理解我
and if you were ever truly my friend, you'll understand.

430
00:15:17,420 --> 00:15:18,640
你们俩逊爆了
You both suck!

431
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:20,460
你们才逊
You suck.

432
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,040
好了 来吧
All right, come on.

433
00:15:23,549 --> 00:15:24,860
我把她放后座上吧
Okay, I'll -- I'll put her in back,

434
00:15:24,860 --> 00:15:27,140
别担心 她很温顺的
and, um, don't worry -- she's really friendly.

435
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,320
我才不怕小羊羊呢
I ain't afraid of no goats.

436
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,640
行 把合同发过来吧
Okay, send me the contracts.

437
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,380
我从来都抗拒不了高颜值的脸蛋
I never could resist a pretty face.

438
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:33,960
别贫了 乔治 我可已经结婚了
Stop it, George. I'm married.

439
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:35,540
我要去趟洗手间
I'm gonna run to the men's room.

440
00:15:38,315 --> 00:15:40,600
你还好吗 一言不发的
So, everything all right? You've barely said a word.

441
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:42,180
反正你不需要我帮忙
Well, it's not like you needed my help,

442
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:44,640
而且我今天出的糗已经够多了
and I think I embarrassed myself enough for one day.

443
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:47,400
听着 我以前可能对你太苛刻了
Look, I might have been too hard on you before.

444
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,820
我只是太厌倦
I'm just tired of everyone

445
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:51,720
所有人不停地拿衣柜点子轰炸我
always pitching me their closet ideas.

446
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:54,340
如果每听一次"下一个最赞衣柜"的点子
If I had a nickel for every time someone came to me

447
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:55,620
我都能收到一枚硬币的话
with "the next great closet",

448
00:15:56,040 --> 00:16:00,280
我都能把它们塞满这个珀耳塞斯系列大衣柜了
I'd have a Pegasus series split-level walk-in full of nickels.

449
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:02,640
但是老爸 我入了这一行
But, Dad, I'm in the biz.

450
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:05,060
早该知道那些都是老掉牙的设计方案
I should have known that those are old design ideas.

451
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,440
没有人能一蹴而就
No one nails it on the first try.

452
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:09,320
我曾经设计过一款蚌壳式鞋盒
Hell, I once pitched a clamshell shoe container

453
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:11,240
上面还有活动铰链呢
with a living hinge.

454
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,172
-不是吧 -我那会儿太嫩了
- No. - I was young.

455
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:15,820
别放弃
Keep with it.

456
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,180
你一定会成功的
You'll get there eventually.

457
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:18,420
谢谢你
Thanks.

458
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:19,800
都吃好了吗
We all set?

459
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:20,780
我去买单
Let me settle up.

460
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:23,500
谢谢你 老爸
Thanks, Dad.

461
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,040
午餐还不错吧
Pretty exciting lunch, huh?

462
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:28,307
沙拉还是照旧的凯撒沙拉
The same caesar salad,

463
00:16:28,307 --> 00:16:29,264
衣柜也还是我年年订的那批衣柜
the same closets I order every year.

464
00:16:29,264 --> 00:16:30,940
没错 但是你也满意吧
Yeah, but you're happy with them, right?

465
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:32,640
不过是衣柜而已
They're closets.

466
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:37,080
如果你想开阔一下眼界
I-if you're ever looking to expand your horizons a little,

467
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:42,400
我也有一些比较新颖别致的设计想法
I have some design ideas that are fresh of the drawing board.

468
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,580
很对不起 我的天
I'm sorry. Oh, gosh.

469
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:45,060
这些是我老公的鸟食
That's my husband's birdseed.

470
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:47,080
我想给你看看这个设计
I'd love to give you a look-see here.

471
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,240
我来收拾这摊
I'll take care of this.

472
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:49,560
老天
Heavens.

473
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:50,810
鸭金汉宫
"Duckingham palace"?

474
00:16:50,810 --> 00:16:52,400
错了 错了 对不起
Oh, no, no. No, no, sorry.

475
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:53,360
不是这些
Those are the wrong ones.

476
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,649
不是这些方案
Um, wrong plans.

477
00:16:54,649 --> 00:16:57,316
我还有别的方案 特别棒
I've got other ones, and they're -- they're super.

478
00:16:59,348 --> 00:17:00,080
老天啊
oh, gosh.

479
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:02,180
天哪 它在我头上是吧
Oh, my god. What -- it's -- it's on my head, right?

480
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:03,600
它在我头上
It's on my head. Okay.

481
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,880
-天 它在我头上 -我的天
- God. Okay. I know it's in here. It's in here. - Oh, my god.

482
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,100
好了 快走开
Okay. Okay.

483
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:08,220
跑到我衬衫里了
Oh, it's in my shirt.

484
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:10,527
-我不过走开了三十秒 -老爸 救我
- I was gone for 30 seconds. - Dad, Dad!

485
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:13,540
也太久了吧
Well, that was forever.

486
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:14,900
太糗了
I'm so embarrassed.

487
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:16,980
我从来没那么紧张过
I've never freaked out like that.

488
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,500
很差劲吗
How bad was it?

489
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:19,960
也就...
I mean...

490
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:22,340
很抱歉我在你不敢跟切尔西说话这件事
I'm so sorry that I gave you such a hard time

491
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:23,900
给你施了那么大压力
about not talking to Chelsea.

492
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,320
其实 你算是帮了我的忙
Actually, you kind of helped me out.

493
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:27,160
为什么
How?

494
00:17:27,620 --> 00:17:29,320
看见你如此反常
Seeing you fall apart like that...

495
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:30,463
结结巴巴 手足无措地说个不停
stutter, twitch, and babble --

496
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:31,240
够了 哔哔
Okay, bloop-bloop.

497
00:17:31,850 --> 00:17:34,370
你是这世上最自信的女人
You're the most confident woman in the world,

498
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:36,220
如果像你这样的人也会像常人一样气馁
and if someone like you can be human,

499
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,740
那我在姑娘面前畏首畏尾也不会觉得难受了
then I don't have to feel bad about chickening out with girls.

500
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,920
你知道谁也是常人吗 切尔西
You know who else is human? Chelsea.

501
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:43,360
所以你又为什么要怕她呢
So why do you feel so intimidated by her?

502
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:44,520
去吧 去找她
Go. Go over there.

503
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:45,740
没时间了
There's no time.

504
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:47,480
周六她五点就下班了
She gets off at 5:00 on saturday

505
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:48,940
这样才赶得及拿完干洗的衣服
so that she can pick up her dry cleaning

506
00:17:49,478 --> 00:17:51,020
去上六点的瑜伽课
and make 6:00 yoga.

507
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:51,420
跟踪狂
Stalker.

508
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:53,180
打电话给她
Call her.

509
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:53,800
真的吗
Really?

510
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:55,520
是的 你可以的
Yes. You can do it.

511
00:17:56,957 --> 00:17:58,226
好吧
Okay.

512
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:01,720
切尔西你好
Hi, Chelsea?

513
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,760
我刚到店里去过 穿着一件绿色夹克
I was in earlier, wearing the green jacket

514
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,120
比被自己剧本逗笑那人还吵[俗丽]
that's louder than that guy laughing at his own screenplay?

515
00:18:06,587 --> 00:18:07,560
她被逗笑了
She's laughing!

516
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:09,720
我希望有时间可以跟你一起喝杯咖啡
I would like to take you out for coffee sometime,

517
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,740
也许去一个不用你来冲咖啡的地方
maybe at a place you don't have to make it?

518
00:18:12,014 --> 00:18:14,180
好极了 好的 明天见
Great. O-okay, I'll see you tomorrow.

519
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:14,580
回见
Bye.

520
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,280
她同意了
She said yes.

521
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:17,680
她当然会同意
Of course she did.

522
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,080
我真为你骄傲
I'm so proud of you.

523
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:21,520
看见了吧 这才是个自信的人会做的事
You see, that's what it is to be a confident person.

524
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:24,080
这些都是由你的母亲遗传给你的
And you got all of it from your mother.

525
00:18:25,824 --> 00:18:27,217
玛...
Mam -- ay!

526
00:18:28,814 --> 00:18:31,045
她叫什么来着
Ay, what's her name?!

527
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:32,660
什么型号的管子
What size tubing would I need

528
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:34,920
能让三只小鸭子滑过去
for three ducklings to slide through?

529
00:18:34,929 --> 00:18:36,540
钱不是问题 你去哪里
Cost is no ob-- where are you going?

530
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:38,800
去后面找一找吗 非常感谢
To the back to check on it? Thank you so much!

531
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:44,200
看哪 你像个真正的孩子一样在玩石头
Well, look at you playing with rocks just like a real kid.

532
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,060
没错
Yep.

533
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,740
我希望那些蛋没事
Oh, I hope those eggs are doing okay.

534
00:18:48,140 --> 00:18:49,500
把它们自己留在家我很过意不去
I feel bad leaving them alone.

535
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,600
也许那样会更安全
Probably safer that way.

536
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:53,480
我知道别人都觉得我疯了
I know people think I'm crazy.

537
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:56,460
我觉得相信别人都不相信的事特别有意思
It's just more fun believing even when no one else does.

538
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:57,700
谁都可以成为怀疑论者
Anyone can be a doubter.

539
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,500
我跟你说过怎么弄到它们的吗
Did I ever tell you how I got them?

540
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:00,520
没有 不过...
No, but I, uh...

541
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:03,660
它们被遗弃在某人的后院 可怜的小东西
I found them abandoned in someone's yard, the poor things.

542
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:04,620
没有母亲
No mother.

543
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:06,260
没有人照顾它们
No one to take care of them.

544
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:09,240
它们是孤儿吗
So, they're orphans?

545
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,560
它们的母亲去哪了
Where did their mother go?

546
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:12,600
我不知道
I don't know.

547
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,480
我只知道它们现在只有我了
I know I'm all they have now.

548
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:19,640
-喂 -喂 亲爱的
- Hello. - Hey, honey.

549
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:21,440
-能帮我个小忙吗 -好
- Can I ask you a tiny little favor? - Okay.

550
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:23,800
能把那些蛋转九十度吗 顺时针转
Can you rotate the eggs 90 degrees, clockwise?

551
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,840
不 菲尔 我不能
No, Phil, I can't. I can't.

552
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:28,260
我累死了 而且我满身是汗
I am tired, and I am sweaty,

553
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:32,220
尽管我这一整天都试图像你一样保持乐观
and as much as I have tried to stay positive like you all day,

554
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:35,000
但是我觉得有时候还是应该面对现实
I think sometimes we need to just face certain facts

555
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,920
比如总部的人不会有创造性
like corporate people are not creative,

556
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,980
比如鸭蛋一个月孵不出来也许就永远也不行了
and ducks that haven't hatched in a month might never.

557
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:42,900
把蛋转一下不就得了 老姑
Just turn the eggs, lady!

558
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:44,540
说真的
You know what?

559
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:46,600
我今天受够鸟类的气了
Kind of done with birds for the day.

560
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:49,960
天哪 菲尔
Oh, my god, Phil.

561
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,320
-好像孵化出来了 -等等 什么
- I think it's hatching. - Wait, what?

562
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:52,200
你确定吗
Are you sure?

563
00:19:52,807 --> 00:19:54,101
我该 该做什么
What -- what do I do?

564
00:19:54,101 --> 00:19:55,543
好 保持冷静
Okay, uh, stay calm.

565
00:19:55,543 --> 00:19:56,860
我会教你分娩
I-I'll talk you through the labor.

566
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:57,660
要生了 莉莉
They're coming, Lily!

567
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:00,820
好吧 克莱尔 告诉你看到什么了
Okay, Claire -- tell me what you see!

568
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:02,140
天哪 我好像看到鸭嘴了
Oh, God. I think I see a beak.

569
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:04,069
好消息是不是脚先出 可以顺产
Well, the good news is we're not breach.

570
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:05,700
它们看起来像是在努力破壳而出
It looks like it's struggling to break through.

571
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:08,560
如果你担心会吓到到它
Okay, if you are concerned about traumatizing him,

572
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:11,120
穿上去年万圣节我们装扮成麦片代言卡通人物
strap on that toucan beak I wore last Halloween

573
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:13,060
我的那套犀鸟服 帮它们把壳啄开
when we dressed as froot loops and start pecking.

574
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:14,820
我还是用叉子吧
I'm using a fork.

575
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:16,266
手别抖 克莱尔 拜托
Steady hands, Claire, please.

576
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,480
我见过你玩"手术"
I've seen you play "Operation".

577
00:20:17,915 --> 00:20:19,960
孵出来了
Oh, it's hatched!

578
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:20,840
太可爱了
It's so cute.

579
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:22,380
太可爱了
Oh, it's so cute!

580
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:23,680
不敢相信我居然错过了
I can't believe I'm missing this!

581
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:24,600
快让开
Hey, buddy!

582
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,420
对外要宣称我当时在场
We're telling people I was there!

583
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:27,600
我觉得另一只也要孵化了
I think another one's hatching.

584
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:29,500
什么 对不起 莉莉
What?! I'm sorry, Lily.

585
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,960
飞跃减速带 三 二...
Speed bump in three, two...

586
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,980
天哪 三只都出来了
Oh, my god, all three?!

587
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,220
太棒了
That's amazing!

588
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,980
-莉莉 拍张照 -好
- Lily, take a picture! - Yep.

589
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:41,100
好了
Here.

590
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:42,680
小家伙
Hi, buddy.

591
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:44,480
准备好了吗
Okay, ready?

592
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,920
一 二
One, two --

593
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:46,960
稍等
Hold up, hold up.

594
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:47,900
它进我衣服里了
He's in my shirt.

595
00:20:48,021 --> 00:20:50,109
鸟怎么总爱往我衣服里钻
Another bird in my shirt.

596
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:51,040
出来了
Got it.

597
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:58,340
我要去睡了 晚安 宝贝
I'm going to bed. Good night, sweetie.

598
00:20:58,940 --> 00:21:00,500
晚安 等等
Good night. Wait. You know what?

599
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:01,760
我刚才在想
I was just thinking,

600
00:21:02,288 --> 00:21:04,691
如果那些鸭蛋都能孵出小鸭...
if those duck eggs were still viable...

601
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,880
也许我们应该去找找
Maybe we should find out if you've got

602
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,880
看你那还有没有一两只蛋[卵]也能孵化出来
one or two fighters left in there, too.

603
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:10,020
不 免了吧
No, thank you.

604
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:13,280
我受够了有小东西在家里跑来跑去的了
I'm done with little ones running around the house.

605
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:16,180
别跟着
Stay.

606
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,360
我说了 别跟着
Oh, I said stay.

607
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,195
那些鸭子把克莱尔当成妈妈了
The ducks imprinted on Claire.

608
00:21:21,066 --> 00:21:22,902
没什么大不了的
It's n-not a big deal.

609
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:25,240
拜托 伙计们
Come on, guys.

610
00:21:25,260 --> 00:21:26,220
她都说了 别跟着
She said stay!

611
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:29,900
拜托
Come on.
